{"name":"Rusty Sword","hex":"#a4493d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rusty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Marked or corroded by rust. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of the rust color, reddish or reddish-brown."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gun or in particular an old or worn one."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rusty"},{"term":"sword","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together forming a hilt), which is designed to cut, stab, slash and/or hack.","A suit in certain playing card decks, particularly those used in Spain and Italy, or those used for divination.\nA card of this suit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stab or cut with a sword"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sword","blocks":[{"text":"A sword is an edged, bladed weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting. Its blade, longer than that of a knife or dagger, is attached to a hilt and can be straight or curved. A thrusting sword tends to have a straighter blade with a pointed tip. A slashing sword is more likely to be curved and to have a sharpened cutting edge on one or both sides of the blade. Many swords are designed for both thrusting and slashing. The precise definition of a sword varies by historical epoch and geographic region."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword","wikidata":"Q12791"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swiss longsword, 15th or 16th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspadon-Morges.jpg"},{"srcse